[Music]  hi I'm Simone de LaRue creator of body  by Simone I decided I wanted to hang up  my dancing heels and segue into fitness  I wanted to bring the love of dance and  the creativity and the freedom and the  joy to as many women as possible so  obviously I trained a lot of celebrities  Jennifer Garner is one of my favorites  that I've been with for four years now  honestly one of the nicest people I have  ever met probably one of the only women  I will get up at 5:00 a.m. every morning  to go and train her for especially when  she was training for her film peppermint  obviously Chrissy Teigen I dream it for  three or four years we do more laughing  than working out to be honest she's Anna  larious person and I liked having a  giggle with her sticking to a workout  plan is tough yeah we always start off  strong we're out the gate really strong  and then we kind of dwindle down when we  realize oh my goodness this is actually  hard work my advice is there is no quick  fix oh yes it is hard work so one thing  you can do is keep an exercise journal  you can have a workout buddy to keep you  accountable if you know you have to be  there and see that workout buddy at 7:00  a.m. and not let them down that's really  going to help motivate you as well and I  always say to every client choose a goal  whether that's the Oscars whether that's  a red carpet whether that's a movie role  whatever that goal is for you set it so  then you've got something to work  towards and that will keep you  accountable and that will also keep you  motivated for me the driving force is  music that's what really motivates me  and that's what motivates you in dance  because obviously you're working to a  rhythm to timing to an 8-count  so like crank on some tunes I always say  to a client picked up a playlist  whatever music you love and that will be  different for everybody but whatever  mode of a  so you put those tunes on because  immediately it's going to put you in a  good mood and it's gonna motivate you  some of the mistakes that people make  when working out is to actually not  research how to do the exercise  correctly I'll often walk into a gym and  see people using heavy weights lifting  heavy weights using machinery that they  they haven't done any research for so  I'd always say if you can at least get a  personal trainer at least once to teach  you how to use the machines and teach  you and give you a program because you  need to use correct technique and  correct form you could do the exercise  for a hundred reps and not use correct  technique and form and end up injuring  yourself and you're not actually going  to see any change in your body for me  health and wellness is not just a quick  fix  it's not the latest fad or the latest  workout it is a lifestyle choice and a  lifestyle change it's not just oh I've  got to work out I'm gonna try and wiener  push through for an hour every day and  then you know change my diet immediately  that's setting yourself up for failure  my philosophy is yes you can have a good  time yes you can have wine every now and  then but we want to balance that with  you know good eating good exercise and a  good mindset meditation and sleep will  set you up for a perfect life  [Music]

